      "finding": "The client rendered Headquarters' Training Day offer at Alia Das arrival. Clicking its Accept Mission button accepted mission 1526; the copied DB records mission 1526 active while Calling for Reinforcements 1995 remains active with its objectives complete."
    },
    {
      "tier": "measured",
      "source_location": "s5-rogers-route-agent-17/step2-southwest-3.png through step4-southwest-9.png; run-s5-rogers-route-agent-17-20260924.py",
      "uncertainty": "Client .where display precision about 0.01 m; held-key duration varies with frame rate and terrain.",
      "finding": "From arrival (+884.109,306.011,+347.809), ordinary S-key movement for three 3-second segments reached approximately (+875.504,299.563,+357.363), (+863.230,295.179,+368.773), and (+853.625,294.016,+378.868), alive. The last screenshot shows a HEADQUARTERS sign; inferred seeded Rogers (+855.84,294.14,+387.4) is about 8.8 m away horizontally."
    },
    {
      "tier": "observed",
      "source_location": "s5-rogers-route-agent-18/19/21 game.log and playable-probe.png; run-s5-rogers-route-agent-21-20260924.py",
      "finding": "After manually restoring only the ordinary-reached run-17 coordinate in the copied character DB, runs 18 and 19 timed out at the harness's 60-second HUD check. A copied long-wait harness in run 21 still showed Wilderness entering-battle loading at 110 seconds; the server received MapLoaded near the end of that window. Run 20 stopped when its orchestrator's 80-second command wait expired before its 110-second HUD wait. No further ordinary movement, Rogers conversation or mission turn-in was observed in these continuation attempts."
    }
  ],
  "assessment": "The original client normally accepted Training Day and traversed from the Alia Das arrival to near Rogers' command tent by ordinary movement. The final 8.8 m, conversation and 1995 turn-in remain unverified by this route because later copied-client logins did not render playable HUD within the tested wait. Earlier separate diagnostic evidence in docs/evidence/client-reinforcements-handoff.json validates a GM-assisted Rogers turn-in, but it does not establish this ordinary route completion. The HUD timeout may reflect heavy client loading; this evidence does not identify a server defect.",
